        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Ln(acac)3·2H2O (0.03 mmol; Ln = Lu for 1) was dissolved in 15 mL of acetonitrile. Then 5 mL of a CH2Cl2 solution of HL (0.0071 g, 0.03 mmol) was added to the stirred acetonitrile solution, and the mixture was stirred for 4 h at room temperature. The solution was filtered. Yellow block crystals suitable for single-crystal X-ray diffraction were isolated by keeping the filtrate at ambient conditions for a few days.",
